// Local adaptation to observed Swiss temperatures - v1.3
// An individual's phenotype is the number of m2 mutations it carries
//
// v1 change: temperature is no longer used as the optimum directly.
// A temperature-to-allele scale maps degrees C onto optimal m2 copies:
//   lowest 1940-1970 mean baseline temp          -> 2.0 optimal m2 copies
//   highest temp in the final observed year      -> 6.0 optimal m2 copies
// Every population therefore starts on a historical optimum near the
// bottom of the scale and must track its own final optimum, with the
// warmest final-year population requiring exactly 6.0 copies.
//
// v1.1 change: the model estimates and logs the effective population
// size, Ne, following SLiM manual section 9.11 ("Effective population
// size versus census population size"):
//   - Heterozygosity Ne = pi / (4 * mu), from NEUTRAL (m1 ) mutations
//     only, per population and for the metapopulation. Backward-looking;
//     needs the burn-in to equilibrate before it is quantitatively
//     meaningful.
//   - Inbreeding Ne (Waples 2002) from the mean and variance of realized
//     fecundity in the parental generation, adapted for this nonWF model
//     (non-overlapping generations; parental pedigree IDs stored
//     explicitly because viability selection makes ID ranges
//     non-contiguous). Instantaneous; responds immediately.
//
// v1.2 changes (thesis support: Ne as a predictor of population decline,
// cf. Hoban et al. 2020 Biol. Conserv. 248:108654, indicator Ne > 500):
//
//   1. PER-POPULATION inbreeding Ne. Offspring migrate before the
//      census, but each parent's deme at reproduction is known (adults
//      are killed before migration, so a parent's subpopulation at the
//      previous census IS where it reproduced). Parental fecundities are
//      therefore grouped by PARENTAL deme and the Waples estimator is
//      applied within each group. Note Hoban et al. (Box 2) caution that
//      local Ne values do not sum to the metapopulation Ne, and that
//      with multiple migrants per generation the Ne > 500 threshold is
//      meant for the whole functional metapopulation.
//
//   2. Phenotypic variance logged per population and in total. The
//      phenotype is entirely genetic here (m2 copy count), so var(tagF)
//      is the genetic variance available to track the moving optimum -
//      the mechanistic link between Ne at time t and census N at t + x.
//
//   3. OPTIONAL reproductive skew, defineConstant("fecunditySkewSD").
//      Default 0.0 reproduces v1.1 behavior exactly. If > 0, each
//      parent's expected litter size R is multiplied by a lognormal
//      deviate with mean 1 (mu = -sd^2/2), adding among-individual
//      variance in reproductive success. This lowers Ne/N below 1
//      toward empirically realistic values (median Ne/Nc across taxa is
//      roughly 0.1; Frankham 1995, cited in Hoban et al.). Measured in
//      test runs: sd = 1.5 gives realized local Ne/N of about 0.2-0.35
//      (mates are still drawn uniformly, which damps the paternal-side
//      variance); raise sd toward ~2.5 to push Ne/N near 0.1. With the
//      default 0.0, reproduction is near-ideal (Poisson) and inbreeding
//      Ne tracks census N almost exactly, so Ne > 500 degenerates to
//      N > 500; skew makes the indicator informative.
//
//
//v1.3
//   1. The disturbance is set by three constants: targetPop (the
//      populations hit), survival (fraction of their individuals left)
//      and habitat (fraction of their K left, for good). These cover
//      every severity of the cluster experiment:
//        halve                       survival 0.5  habitat 0.5
//        severe                      survival 0.1  habitat 0.1
//        bottleneck                  survival 0.1  habitat 1
//        destroy, recolonisable      survival 0    habitat 1
//        destroy, no recolonisation  survival 0    habitat 0  (a sink)
//      targetPop = c() runs without a disturbance.
//   2. Each population has its own K (popK), so a disturbance can lower
//      the K of one population only.
//   3. One log, written with a LogFile (SLiM manual section 4.2.5), in long
//      format: one row per population per tick. The columns are the
//      same as the cluster experiment's logs, minus temporal Ne and the
//      population name (location), and the number of columns does not
//      grow with the number of populations.
//   4. The same model as grib_ramp_v1.2_disturbance.slim (the cluster
//      script): with the same settings and seed it gives the same run.
//
// Reproduction
// Reproduction of the whole population in one callback (SLiM's pattern for
// population-level reproduction in nonWF models). The callback runs for the
// first individual only, produces the offspring of every population, then
// switches itself off for the rest of the tick (self.active = 0).
//   Step 1: how many offspring a population produces: Poisson around
//           R x N, as if every individual had one litter. Reproductive
//           skew does not change this number, so it cannot make the
//           population size crash.
//   Step 2: who the parents are. Each individual has a fecundity (a
//           lognormal value with mean 1, e.g. condition or body size).
//           The first parent of each offspring is chosen in proportion to
//           fecundity, so high-fecundity individuals leave more offspring.
// With fecunditySkewSD = 0 every individual has fecundity 1, which gives
// the same offspring numbers per individual as v1.4 (Poisson, Ne close to N).
//
// Requires initializeSLiMOptions(keepPedigrees=T) for pedigree IDs.
// Output: <outputDirectory>/run_<RUN>_log.csv, one row per population per tick.
//
// Cluster version: every setting that differs between runs is read from
// row RUN of run_matrix_1000.csv, and the migration and climate files are
// migration_matrices/run_<RUN>.csv and climate_matrices/run_<RUN>.csv.
// Populations p0, p1, ... are the cities of pop_ids in order; the log's
// "city" column gives the city number of each population.


initialize(){
	initializeSLiMModelType("nonWF");
	initializeSLiMOptions(keepPedigrees=T);
	
	/** **Cluster Instructions** */
	///Run settings
	//These three can be set from the command line, ex:
	//slim -d RUN=2 -d "INPUT_DIR='/path/to/14102026/'" -d "OUTPUT_DIR='/path/to/results/'" model.slim
	//If they are not set (e.g. in SLiMgui), the values below are used.
	if (!exists("RUN"))
		defineConstant("RUN", 1);//which row of the run matrix to run
	if (!exists("INPUT_DIR"))
		defineConstant("INPUT_DIR", "C:/Users/WilliamWallisch/msc_workspace/SLiM/input/grib_pop_index_local_adaptation/run_repo/14102026/");
	if (!exists("OUTPUT_DIR"))
		defineConstant("OUTPUT_DIR", "C:/Users/WilliamWallisch/msc_workspace/SLiM/results/ramp_v1.3.1_cluster/");
		
	/** **Constants/Inputs/Outputs** */
	///Input files (all inside INPUT_DIR, the files for this run picked by RUN)
	defineConstant("inputDirectory", INPUT_DIR);
	defineConstant("migrationFile", inputDirectory + "migration_matrices/run_" + RUN + ".csv");
	defineConstant("climateFile", inputDirectory + "climate_matrices/run_" + RUN + ".csv");
	defineConstant("yearFile", inputDirectory + "climate_years/grib_climate_years_8pop_1940_2025.csv");
	defineConstant("masterFile", inputDirectory + "run_matrix_1000.csv");
	
	///Output files (one log per run)
	defineConstant("outputDirectory", OUTPUT_DIR);
	defineConstant("logFile", outputDirectory + "run_" + RUN + "_log.csv");
	
	///Read this run's row of the run matrix
	runTable = readCSV(masterFile);
	runRow = runTable.subsetRows(which(runTable.getValue("run") == RUN));
	
	if (runRow.nrow != 1)
		stop("Run " + RUN + " was not found exactly once in " + masterFile);
	
	//City number of each population, in order: p0 is the first city in pop_ids, p1 the second, ...
	//(the same order as the rows of the migration file and the columns of the climate file)
	//City numbers: 0 geneva, 1 lausanne, 2 neuchatel, 3 bern, 4 solothurn, 5 lucerne, 6 winterthur, 7 stgallen
	defineConstant("popCities", asInteger(strsplit(asString(runRow.getValue("pop_ids")), ";")));
	
	//Cities hit by the disturbance ("" = none), turned into population positions (p0, p1, ...)
	targetText = asString(runRow.getValue("target_pops"));
	
	if ((targetText == "") | (targetText == "none"))
		targetCities = integer(0);
	else
		targetCities = asInteger(strsplit(targetText, ";"));
	
	targetPositions = match(targetCities, popCities);
	
	if (any(targetPositions < 0))
		stop("A target city is not one of this run's populations.");
	
	//Read the migration data
	migrationTable = readCSV(migrationFile, colNames=F);
	migrationInput = migrationTable.asMatrix();
	print(migrationInput);//show the matrix
	
	//Read the climate data
	climateTable = readCSV(climateFile, colNames=F);
	climateInput = climateTable.asMatrix();
	
	//Read the climate years
	yearTable = readCSV(yearFile, colNames=F);
	yearMatrix = yearTable.asMatrix();
	yearInput = asInteger(drop(yearMatrix));
	
	//The files must agree with the run matrix
	if ((nrow(migrationInput) != size(popCities)) | (ncol(climateInput) != size(popCities)))
		stop("Run " + RUN + ": the migration or climate file does not have one row/column per population.");
	
	///Main model parameters (from this run's row)
	defineConstant("numPops", nrow(migrationInput));
	defineConstant("migrationMatrix", migrationInput);
	defineConstant("climateMatrix", climateInput);
	defineConstant("climateYears", yearInput);
	defineConstant("K", asInteger(runRow.getValue("K_per_pop")));//K per population
	defineConstant("R", 1.01);
	defineConstant("selectionStrength", asFloat(runRow.getValue("selection_strength")));
	defineConstant("TlocalAdaptation", 4000);//historical mean is reached
	defineConstant("TclimateChange", 8000);//observed climate begins
	
	///Disturbance (from this run's row)
	defineConstant("targetPop", targetPositions);//positions of the populations hit (c() = none)
	defineConstant("survival", asFloat(runRow.getValue("D_inds")));//fraction of individuals left
	defineConstant("habitat", asFloat(runRow.getValue("D_habitat")));//fraction of K left (0 = habitat gone, no recolonisation)
	defineConstant("disturbanceLag",0);//ticks before climate change
	defineConstant("Tdisturb", TclimateChange - disturbanceLag);// also used for the phase label
	defineConstant("isDisturbed", (size(targetPop) > 0) & ((survival < 1.0) | (habitat < 1.0)));
	
	catn("Run " + RUN + " | seed " + getSeed() + " | cities " + paste(popCities, sep=",") +
		" | K per pop " + K + " | selection " + selectionStrength +
		" | target cities " + paste(targetCities, sep=",") + " | survival " + survival + " | habitat " + habitat);
	
	//Field proxy
	defineConstant("neProxyRatio", 0.1);//Ne proxy = 0.1 x census N (field rule of thumb)
	
	//0.0 = ideal Poisson reproduction, Ne/N near 1
	//2.5–3 gives Ne/N roughly 0.1
	defineConstant("fecunditySkewSD", 0.0);
	
	///Mutation and Alleles
	//v1.1: mutation-rate constants, needed by the heterozygosity Ne estimator (Ne = pi / (4 * mu), with mu the NEUTRAL rate)
	defineConstant("overallMutationRate", 1e-7);
	defineConstant("neutralFraction", 0.99);//proportion of mutations that are m1; also used in neutralMutationRate
	defineConstant("neutralMutationRate", overallMutationRate * neutralFraction);
	
	//Temperature-to-allele scale anchors
	defineConstant("startAlleleOptimum", 2.0);
	defineConstant("endAlleleOptimum", 6.0);
	
	///Climate Years
	//Find the historical years and observed climate years
	historicalRows = which((climateYears >= 1940) & (climateYears <= 1970));
	observedRows = which(climateYears >= 1970);
	
	//Calculate the historical mean temperature for every population
	historicalMeans = apply(climateMatrix[historicalRows, ],1,"mean(applyValue);");
	
	defineConstant("historicalMeanClimate", historicalMeans);
	defineConstant("observedClimateRows", observedRows);
	defineConstant("numObservedYears", size(observedRows));
	defineConstant("Tend", TclimateChange + numObservedYears - 1);
	
	//Temperatures of the final observed climate year
	finalClimateRow = observedRows[size(observedRows) - 1];
	finalTemperatures = drop(climateInput[finalClimateRow,]);
	
	///Temperature
	//Anchor the scale on the coldest historical baseline mean and the warmest temperature of the final observed year
	defineConstant("startTemperature", min(historicalMeans));
	defineConstant("endTemperature", max(finalTemperatures));
	defineConstant("finalClimate", finalTemperatures);
	
	//The optimum every population must reach by the historical mean phase
	defineConstant("historicalAlleleOptima",
		temperatureToAlleleOptimum(historicalMeanClimate));
	
	
	///Genetics
	initializeMutationRate(overallMutationRate);
	initializeRecombinationRate(1e-8);
	initializeMutationType("m1", 0.5, "f", 0.0);//neutral mutations
	initializeMutationType("m2", 0.5, "f", 0.0);//climate phenotype mutations
	m2.convertToSubstitution = F;//mutations that fix will not be replaced
	m2.color = "red";//will be displayed in red in the output
	initializeGenomicElementType("g1", c(m1, m2),
		c(neutralFraction, 1 - neutralFraction));
	initializeGenomicElement(g1, 0, 99999);
	
	///SLiM Gui
	//The optimum every population must track by the final observed year
	defineConstant("finalAlleleOptima",
		temperatureToAlleleOptimum(finalClimate));
	
	catn("Temperature-to-allele scale: " + startTemperature + " C = " +
		startAlleleOptimum + " copies, " + endTemperature + " C = " +
		endAlleleOptimum + " copies.");
	
	for (pop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
		catn("p" + pop +
			" | Historical mean temperature: " + historicalMeanClimate[pop] +
			" | Historical allele optimum: " + historicalAlleleOptima[pop] +
			" | Final temperature: " + finalClimate[pop] +
			" | Final allele optimum: " + finalAlleleOptima[pop] + ".");
	}
	
	if (isDisturbed)
		catn("Disturbance at tick " + Tdisturb + ": populations " + paste(targetPop, sep=", ") +
		" keep " + survival + " of their individuals and " + habitat + " of their K.");
	else
		catn("No disturbance.");
}


/** **Model** */
reproduction()
{
	// (subpop is already taken: inside reproduction() it is the population
	// of the individual the callback was called for)
	for (population in sim.subpopulations)
	{
		parents = population.individuals;
		numParents = size(parents);
		
		// Two different parents are needed
		if (numParents < 2)
			next;
		
		//Step 1: number of offspring
		numOffspring = rpois(1, R * numParents);
		
		if (numOffspring == 0)
			next;
		
		//Step 2: fecundity of each individual
		if (fecunditySkewSD > 0.0)
			fecundity = exp(rnorm(numParents, -fecunditySkewSD^2 / 2, fecunditySkewSD));
		else
			fecundity = rep(1.0, numParents);
		
		// Choose the parents of every offspring (as positions in parents)
		positions = 0:(numParents - 1);
		firstParent = sample(positions, numOffspring, replace=T, weights=fecundity);
		mate = sample(positions, numOffspring, replace=T);
		
		// No selfing: choose a new mate wherever it is the first parent
		selfed = which(mate == firstParent);
		
		while (size(selfed) > 0)
		{
			mate[selfed] = sample(positions, size(selfed), replace=T);
			selfed = selfed[mate[selfed] == firstParent[selfed]];
		}
		
		// Produce the offspring
		for (i in seqLen(numOffspring))
		{
			population.addCrossed(parents[firstParent[i]], parents[mate[i]]);
		}
	}
	
	self.active = 0;
}


///Create the starting populations
1 early(){
	for (pop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
		sim.addSubpop("p" + pop, K);
	}
	
	//Carrying capacity of each population; only a disturbance changes it
	sim.setValue("popK", rep(asFloat(K), numPops));
}


///Demography/migration
1:Tend early(){
	/// Non-overlapping generations
	allIndividuals = sim.subpopulations.individuals;
	adults = allIndividuals[allIndividuals.age > 0];
	
	if (size(adults) > 0)
		sim.killIndividuals(adults);
	
	
	/// Disturbance
	// Once, at Tdisturb, on the new generation before migration.
	// Populations are handled in number order, as in the cluster script, so the same seed gives the same run.
	if (isDisturbed & (sim.cycle == Tdisturb)){
		popK = sim.getValue("popK");
		
		for (pop in sort(targetPop))
		{
			subpop = sim.subpopulations[pop];
			popIntact = subpop.individualCount;
			
			//Kill (1 - survival) of the individuals, chosen at random
			numKilled = asInteger(round(popIntact * (1 - survival)));
			
			if (numKilled > 0)
				sim.killIndividuals(sample(subpop.individuals, numKilled));
			
			//Habitat left for good (0 = a sink: migrants that arrive die)
			popK[pop] = K * habitat;
			
			catn("Disturbance at tick " + sim.cycle + ": p" + pop + " " +
				popIntact + " -> " + subpop.individualCount + ", K now " + popK[pop] + ".");
		}
		
		sim.setValue("popK", popK);
	}
	
	
	//Migration
	//First choose every migrant without moving anyone
	allMigrants = c();
	allDestinations = c();
	
	for (sourcePop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
		sourceSubpop = sim.subpopulations[sourcePop];
		
		if (sourceSubpop.individualCount == 0)
			next;
		
		//Get the migration rates leaving this population
		migrationRates = drop(migrationMatrix[sourcePop,]);
		migrationRates[sourcePop] = 0.0;
		totalMigrationRate = sum(migrationRates);
		
		if (totalMigrationRate > 1.0)
			stop("Migration rate above 1.");
		
		if (totalMigrationRate == 0.0)
			next;
		
		//Choose how many individuals migrate
		numMigrants = rbinom(1, sourceSubpop.individualCount,
			totalMigrationRate);
		
		if (numMigrants == 0)
			next;
		
		//Choose the migrants and their destinations
		popMigrants = sample(sourceSubpop.individuals, numMigrants);
		popDestinations = sample(0:(numPops - 1), numMigrants,
			replace=T, weights=migrationRates);
		
		allMigrants = c(allMigrants, popMigrants);
		allDestinations = c(allDestinations, popDestinations);
	}
	
	//Move the migrants after every migration choice has been made
	if (size(allMigrants) > 0){
		for (destinationPop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
			migrants = allMigrants[allDestinations == destinationPop];
			
			if (size(migrants) > 0)
				sim.subpopulations[destinationPop].takeMigrants(migrants);
		}
	}
	
	///Local Adaptation
	//Phase 1: ticks 1-1999 gradually approach each historical optimum
	if (sim.cycle < TlocalAdaptation){
		adaptProgress = asFloat(sim.cycle) / TlocalAdaptation;
		climates = historicalMeanClimate;
		alleleOptima = historicalAlleleOptima * adaptProgress;
		currentYear = "Local Adaptation";
	}
	
	//Phase 2: ticks 2000-3999 remain at each historical optimum
	else if (sim.cycle < TclimateChange){
		climates = historicalMeanClimate;
		alleleOptima = historicalAlleleOptima;
		currentYear = "Historical Mean";
	}
	
	//Phase 3: tick 4000 begins the observed climate record with 1970
	else{
		climateYearIndex = sim.cycle - TclimateChange;
		
		if (climateYearIndex >= numObservedYears)
			climateYearIndex = numObservedYears - 1;
		
		//observedClimateRows = c(30 (1970), 31, 32, 33...);
		climateRow = observedClimateRows[climateYearIndex];
		climates = drop(climateMatrix[climateRow,]);
		alleleOptima = temperatureToAlleleOptimum(climates);
		currentYear = asString(climateYears[climateRow]);
		
		//tick 4000, climateYearIndex 0, calendar year 1970
	}
	
	///Climate fitness
	inds = sim.subpopulations.individuals;
	popK = sim.getValue("popK");
	
	if (size(inds) > 0){
		phenotypes = asFloat(inds.countOfMutationsOfType(m2));
		popIDs = inds.subpopulation.id;
		popOptima = alleleOptima[popIDs];
		
		fitness = 1.0 - (phenotypes - popOptima)^2 * selectionStrength;
		fitness[fitness < 0.0] = 0.0;
		
		inds.fitnessScaling = fitness;
		inds.tagF = phenotypes;
		
		//Mean fitness per population, for the log. A sink (K = 0) holds only arriving migrants that are about to die, so it gets NA.
		for (pop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
			popFitness = fitness[popIDs == pop];
			hasValue = (size(popFitness) > 0) & (popK[pop] > 0);
			sim.setValue("meanFitness_p" + pop, hasValue ? mean(popFitness) else NULL);
		}
	}
	else{
		for (pop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
			sim.setValue("meanFitness_p" + pop, NULL);
		}
	}
	
	
	///Density Regulation
	//Each population is regulated towards its own K (K = 0: a sink)
	for (subpop in sim.subpopulations){
		if (subpop.individualCount > 0)
			subpop.fitnessScaling = min(popK[subpop.id] / subpop.individualCount, 1.5);
	}
	
	
	//Save climate values for the output event
	sim.setValue("currentClimates", climates);
	sim.setValue("currentAlleleOptima", alleleOptima);
	sim.setValue("currentClimateYear", currentYear);
}

//Finish after the final observed climate year
Tend late(){
	sim.simulationFinished();
}


/** **Output** */
///Log file
1 early()
{
	//v1.4: the log (SLiM manual section 4.2.5, LogFile). logRow() is called once per population per tick (see Tick logging); every column is evaluated again for the population of that row, logRowPop().
	//A column whose value cannot be computed (e.g. Ne of an empty population) is written as NA.
	if (!fileExists(outputDirectory))
		createDirectory(outputDirectory);
	
	log = community.createLogFile(logFile, logInterval=NULL);
	log.addCycle();
	log.addCustomColumn("phase", "currentPhase();");
	log.addCustomColumn("year", "sim.getValue('currentClimateYear');");
	log.addCustomColumn("run", "RUN;");
	log.addCustomColumn("pop", "logRowPop();");
	log.addCustomColumn("city", "popCities[logRowPop()];");//city number of this population
	log.addCustomColumn("N", "sim.subpopulations[logRowPop()].individualCount;");
	log.addCustomColumn("K", "sim.getValue('popK')[logRowPop()];");
	log.addCustomColumn("Ne_het", "subpopNeHeterozygosity(logRowPop());");
	log.addCustomColumn("Ne_inb", "subpopNeInbreeding(logRowPop());");
	log.addCustomColumn("Ne_het_metapop", "sim.getValue('metapopNeHet');");
	log.addCustomColumn("Ne_inb_metapop", "sim.getValue('metapopNeInb');");
	log.addCustomColumn("Ne_proxy", "neProxyRatio * sim.subpopulations[logRowPop()].individualCount;");
	log.addCustomColumn("meanFitness", "sim.getValue('meanFitness_p' + logRowPop());");
	log.addCustomColumn("meanPheno", "subpopMeanPhenotype(logRowPop());");
	log.addCustomColumn("optimum", "sim.getValue('currentAlleleOptima')[logRowPop()];");
	log.addCustomColumn("varPheno", "subpopPhenotypeVariance(logRowPop());");
	
	defineConstant("LOG", log);
	catn("Logging to: " + logFile);
}


///Tick logging
//One log row per population, then record this tick's survivors (IDs and populations) as the parental generation for the next tick's inbreeding Ne. Declared before the console output so a row is written even in thetick in which total extinction is detected.
1:Tend late(){
	// Metapopulation Ne is the same on every row, so compute it once
	sim.setValue("metapopNeHet", metapopNeHeterozygosity());
	sim.setValue("metapopNeInb", metapopNeInbreeding());
	
	for (pop in 0:(numPops - 1)){
		sim.setValue("logRowPop", pop);
		LOG.logRow();
	}
	
	survivors = sim.subpopulations.individuals;
	sim.setValue("previousPedigreeIDs", survivors.pedigreeID);
	sim.setValue("previousSubpopIDs", survivors.subpopulation.id);
}


///Console output
//One line every 100 ticks, and every tick from the disturbance on.
//Stops the run if every population is extinct.
1:Tend late(){
	popSizes = sim.subpopulations.individualCount;
	
	if (sum(popSizes) == 0){
		catn("All populations extinct at tick " + sim.cycle + ".");
		sim.simulationFinished();
	}
	else if ((sim.cycle % 100 == 0) | (sim.cycle >= Tdisturb))
	{
		catn("Tick " + sim.cycle + " | " + sim.getValue("currentClimateYear") +
			" | N: " + paste(popSizes, sep=" "));
	}
}



/** **Functions** */
///Temperature scale
//Temperature in degrees C -> optimal number of m2 copies
function (float) temperatureToAlleleOptimum(float temperatures){
	return startAlleleOptimum +
		(temperatures - startTemperature) *
		(endAlleleOptimum - startAlleleOptimum) /
		(endTemperature - startTemperature);
}


///Ne estimation (SLiM manual section 9.11, adapted for this model)
//Heterozygosity Ne = pi / (4 * mu), using neutral m1 mutations only
function (Nf$) estimateNeHeterozygosity(object<Haplosome> haplosomes){
	if (size(haplosomes) == 0)
		return NULL;
	
	pi = calcHeterozygosity(haplosomes, sim.mutationsOfType(m1));
	return pi / (4 * neutralMutationRate);
}

//Heterozygosity Ne for one population, by index; NULL if extinct
function (Nf$) subpopNeHeterozygosity(integer$ popIndex){
	subpop = sim.subpopulations[popIndex];
	
	if (subpop.individualCount == 0)
		return NULL;
	
	return estimateNeHeterozygosity(subpop.individuals.haplosomes);
}

//Heterozygosity Ne for the whole metapopulation
function (Nf$) metapopNeHeterozygosity(void){
	individuals = sim.subpopulations.individuals;
	
	if (size(individuals) == 0)
		return NULL;
	
	return estimateNeHeterozygosity(individuals.haplosomes);
}

//Number of offspring per parental individual, including zeros for
//parents that left no surviving offspring. parentalIDs must hold the
//pedigree IDs of the full parental generation (last tick's survivors).
function (integer) tabulateFecundity(object<Individual> offspring, integer parentalIDs){
	parentIDs = offspring.pedigreeParentIDs;
	base = min(parentalIDs);
	counts = tabulate(parentIDs - base, max(parentalIDs) - base);
	return counts[parentalIDs - base];
}

//Inbreeding Ne from a fecundity distribution k
//(Waples 2002, as in SLiM manual section 9.11)
function (Nf$) waplesNe(integer k){
	numParents = size(k);
	
	if (numParents < 2)
		return NULL;
	
	meanFecundity = mean(k);
	
	if (meanFecundity == 0)
		return NULL;
	
	denominator = meanFecundity - 1 + var(k) / meanFecundity;
	
	if (denominator <= 0)
		return NULL;
	
	return (numParents * meanFecundity - 2) / denominator;
}

//Fecundity distribution of the previous tick's survivors (the parental
//generation), or NULL if it cannot be computed yet
function (Ni) parentalFecundity(void){
	parentalIDs = sim.getValue("previousPedigreeIDs");
	
	//No parental generation recorded yet (tick 1)
	if (isNULL(parentalIDs))
		return NULL;
	
	offspring = sim.subpopulations.individuals;
	
	if ((size(parentalIDs) < 2) | (size(offspring) == 0))
		return NULL;
	
	//Founders have no recorded parents (pedigree parent ID -1)
	if (min(offspring.pedigreeParentIDs) < 0)
		return NULL;
	
	return tabulateFecundity(offspring, parentalIDs);
}

//Inbreeding Ne for the whole metapopulation
function (Nf$) metapopNeInbreeding(void){
	k = parentalFecundity();
	
	if (isNULL(k))
		return NULL;
	
	return waplesNe(k);
}

//v1.2: inbreeding Ne for one population. Parents are grouped by the
//population in which they reproduced (their subpopulation at the
//previous census); their offspring are counted wherever they migrated to.
function (Nf$) subpopNeInbreeding(integer$ popIndex){
	k = parentalFecundity();
	
	if (isNULL(k))
		return NULL;
	
	parentalPops = sim.getValue("previousSubpopIDs");
	return waplesNe(k[parentalPops == popIndex]);
}


///Phenotype (v1.2)
//Variance of the phenotype (m2 copy count) within one population; the phenotype is entirely genetic, so this is the population's genetic variance
//Ne ≈ (4N − 2) / (Vk + 2)
function (Nf$) subpopPhenotypeVariance(integer$ popIndex){
	subpop = sim.subpopulations[popIndex];
	
	if (subpop.individualCount < 2)
		return NULL;
	
	return var(subpop.individuals.tagF);
}

//Mean phenotype of one population (tagF holds the phenotype set this tick)
function (Nf$) subpopMeanPhenotype(integer$ popIndex){
	subpop = sim.subpopulations[popIndex];
	
	if (subpop.individualCount == 0)
		return NULL;
	
	return mean(subpop.individuals.tagF);
}


///Log helpers
//The population whose log row is being written (set in Tick logging)
function (integer$) logRowPop(void){
	return sim.getValue("logRowPop");
}

//Phase label for the log
function (s$) currentPhase(void){
	if (sim.cycle < TlocalAdaptation)
		return "local_adaptation";
	
	if (sim.cycle >= TclimateChange)
		return "climate_change";
	
	if (isDisturbed & (sim.cycle >= Tdisturb))
		return "post_disturbance";
	
	return "historical_hold";
}